      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The idea behind the EM (expectation/maximization) algorithm for variance-component analysis is that if we knew the values of the random effects, we could estimate the variances in a simple fashion directly from them. Focusing on the general mixed model defined by Equation 27.8a, the variances of the random and residual effects are defined respectively to be",
